7. ETHICS AND SAFETY INTEGRITY

Wilson's reference architecture includes mandatory ethics checkpoints and auditability
mechanisms. A distribution presented as "Wilson" or as an official-compatible Wilson
implementation must not disable, bypass, conceal, falsify, or silently remove:

(a) the required ethics checkpoint at every canonical 0,0 condition;
(b) the versioned ethics-policy identifier or policy hash;
(c) the middleware execution audit chain;
(d) the ethics checkpoint audit chain; or
(e) hardware/QPU provenance when such evidence is represented as having been generated.

Modified forks may experiment with alternative ethics policies only if they:

(i) clearly disclose that the policy was modified;
(ii) preserve the original policy and provenance for comparison;
(iii) do not represent the modified policy as the Licensor's canonical policy; and
(iv) do not use the Wilson name or branding in a misleading manner.

